.TH "GLESHA-BROWSE" "1" "" "glesha" "User Commands"
.nh
.ad l
.SH NAME
glesha\-browse \- list the files in a snapshot
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBglesha browse\fR SET [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
List the entries of a snapshot of SET, by default the latest. Without \-\-path the roots are listed; without \-\-recursive only the direct children of the path are listed.
.PP
If the catalog is encrypted and not yet open on this computer, it is downloaded and the catalog passphrase is requested.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-snapshot ID
Snapshot ID, or 'latest' (default: latest).
.TP
.B \-\-path PATH
List entries under PATH (default: the roots).
.TP
.B \-\-recursive
Include all descendants.
.SS Remote options
.TP
.B \-\-to REMOTE...
Limit bucket access to REMOTE.
.TP
.B \-\-from REMOTE...
Limit bucket access to REMOTE.
.PP
REMOTE... takes a comma\-separated list and may be repeated. If \-\-from or \-\-to is given, no other remote is accessed.
.SS Passphrase options
.TP
.B \-\-catalog\-passphrase\-file FILE
Read the catalog passphrase from FILE ('\-': stdin). Without this option, GLESHA_CATALOG_PASSPHRASE or a hidden prompt is used.
.PP
The global options described in glesha(1) are also accepted.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
glesha browse docs
glesha browse docs \-\-path Documents \-\-recursive
glesha browse docs \-\-snapshot ID
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glesha (1),
.BR glesha\-history (1),
.BR glesha\-restore (1)
